      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey can u give me a quick checklist for wcag 2.1 compliance? mostly looking for stuff on color contrast ratios and making sure screen readers work right for a new fintech app we're building",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a brief checklist for WCAG 2.1 compliance in your fintech app:\n\n1. **Color Contrast Ratio**: Ensure color combinations meet WCAG guidelines (14 or higher for normal text and 7 or higher for smaller text, background, and icons).\n2. **Screen Reader Compatibility**:\n\t* Use the Facebook Accessibility Tools or Accessibility Checker to test for screen reader compatibility.\n\t* Ensure focus order, button labels, and form controls are correctly read by screen readers.\n3. **Other essential checks**:\n\t* Provide alternative text for images.\n\t* Ensure navigation and menus are accessible and labeled.\n\t* Correctly implement HTML labels for form controls.\n4. **Keyboard Navigation**: Test keyboard navigation to ensure users can move focus through the app using only the keyboard.\n5. **Semantic HTML**: Use semantic HTML elements (e.g., `<header>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<footer>`) for structure and organization.\n\nSmall steps, aim for full compliance!",
      "source": "target",
